'use strict';

/**
 * bd-31ziu8.3 — the FICO-S v1.1 observation form as ONE WhatsApp Flow (bot/docs/flows/fico-s-flow.json, generated by
 * bot/scripts/generate-fico-s-flow-json.js; FICO_S_FLOW_ID). It shares FDE's endpoint (POST /api/flows/obs612), token
 * (<coachUserId>:obs612:<formId>) and form row; routes/obs612-endpoint.js hands a FICO-S form to handleInit /
 * handleDataExchange here.
 *
 *   FS_START            what FICO-S is and how to score (no input; the screen INIT answers with)
 *   FS_INTRO_<A..E>     each section opens with its question and the indicators in it (no input)
 *   FS_<A..E>_<ONE..>   ONE indicator per screen: its name, what to look for, how; the four levels, each its name and
 *                       the sheet's words (C2 also "N/A · no answer was wrong"); the observer's evidence (required,
 *                       at least 20 characters: the sheet's "write what you saw and heard as evidence")
 *   FS_CHECKLIST        the sheet's 12 Yes/No checks (not scored; every one required, operator 19 Nov: "the checklist
 *                       section is not optional")
 *   FS_FEEDBACK         the score so far (read-only), 1-2 strengths, ONE indicator to work on with an action and a date
 *                       (a second one optional): the sheet's Feedback rule. Submit.
 *   NOTICE / DONE       as FDE's form: refused / the one terminal screen.
 *
 * Every word on a screen is endpoint data in the observer's language (en | ur; Urdu a DRAFT for native review, from
 * frameworks/fico-s/fico_s_v1_1.ur.json), so one published Flow serves both. Meta's rules (whatsapp-flows skill): INIT
 * answers only a screen with no route in (FS_START, NOTICE); routes are forward only, every form screen may also go to
 * DONE; going back is the header arrow (each screen says so); radio label 30, TextArea/TextInput/Dropdown label 20,
 * helper 80, option title 30, description 300, heading 80.
 *
 * Pure (no I/O): the endpoint reads and writes; this module shapes screens and checks answers.
 *
 * Versions (queue #218): every function that shows N/A, a note or the label takes the form's rubric id (`rubric`, from
 * observation_field_forms.rubric_version), so a v1.1 form finishes on v1.1 and a v1.2 one shows v1.2: N/A on C2 and C3
 * in their own words, C3 on N/A when the observer set C1 to 1 (with a note), the C5 / A3 scoring notes. None of it needs a
 * Flow republish: the option lists and the text under each indicator are endpoint data. Default: the current version.
 */

